      "id": 1,
      "text": "Burlington began as a tavern in 1840, a post office in 1846, a general store in 1847 and incorporated in 1906.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://exploreelginarea.com/plan-your-visit/about-explore-elgin-area/communities/burlington-il/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village sits on the former Illinois Central Railroad, which runs through its southern edge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burlington%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1878, Burlington boasted three cheese factories, a general store, a hotel, and a saloon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burlington%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every year, Burlington hosts Holiday Magic on Main Street, the Annual Street Dance, July 3 fireworks, and Fall Fest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://exploreelginarea.com/plan-your-visit/about-explore-elgin-area/communities/burlington-il/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Mott’s Lounge, a 100‑year‑old tavern, draws residents of all ages to cover bands and street dancing during the Annual Street Dance.",
